.SH COMMANDS
.SS status
Offline inventory: shipped sources and their versions, rust toolchain
presence (with the exact remediation hint when missing), libpcap dev
availability, per\-crate build stamps, the built brain binary, and the
canonical brain socket.
Prints the next step for every gap.
Never invokes cargo, never downloads.
.SS toolchain
Installs the build toolchain \(em \f[CR]rustc\f[R], \f[CR]cargo\f[R],
\f[CR]pkg\-config\f[R], \f[CR]libpcap\-dev\f[R] (the pcap crate\(cqs
capture feature links libpcap) \(em via a noninteractive
\f[CR]apt\-get install\f[R].
Needs root and network.
Boxes without apt: the error names the packages instead.
.SS build
\f[CR]cargo build \-\-release \-\-locked\f[R] for each crate, with build
output redirected \f[I]out of the read\-only package tree\f[R] into the
state root (\f[CR]$WORKSPACE_ROOT/rust/target\f[R], default
\f[CR]/var/lib/daharness/rust/target\f[R], daharness\-group shared
2770).
Per\-crate \f[CR][ok]/[\-\-]\f[R] lines; a successful crate drops a
\f[I]crate.build.ok\f[R] stamp (rustc version) that \f[B]status\f[R]
reads.
On a real failure nothing is half\-installed \(em the deb\(cqs python
stack never touches these crates.
\f[I]\(enno\-pcap\f[R] (or \f[CR]DAHARNESS_RUST_NO_PCAP=1\f[R]) builds
the pcap crate\(cqs dependency\-free codec core when the libpcap capture
lane is unwanted; a plain failure on pcap points at the same remedy.
.SS smoke
\f[CR]cargo test \-\-release \-\-locked\f[R] per crate \(em verifies the
ports hold their semantics on \f[I]your\f[R] box (the same suites
upstream CI runs).
A failing suite prints the verbose rerun command and the lane refuses to
declare itself verified.
.SS all
The one\-command upgrade: toolchain && build && smoke.
.SS brain
Runs the rust sidecar lane end\-to\-end: starts the python tool\-worker
(\f[CR]rust/brain/worker.py\f[R], which imports the harness registry and
executes through the shared \f[CR]tool_exec\f[R] core) and then the
compiled brain binary in the foreground.
By default this is a \f[B]private lane\f[R] \(em its own brain and
worker sockets under \f[CR]$WORKSPACE_ROOT/run/\f[R], so it coexists
with the shipped python sidecar.
With \f[I]\(encanonical\f[R] it takes the real Brain socket path
(\f[CR]$BRAIN_SOCKET\f[R] from the profile plumbing, e.g.
\f[CR]/run/daharness/brain.sock\f[R]); a live python sidecar on that
socket is probed first and \f[B]refused\f[R] with
\f[CR]systemctl stop daharness\f[R] \(em the brain binary\(cqs own
flock/connect\-probe singleton guard is the deeper fence against races.
Smoke it from another shell with
\f[CR]python3 /usr/share/daharness/rust/brain/smoke.py <socket>\f[R].
